From: gts9wifi mainline port <gts9-mainline@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom-qmp-pcie: select the PHY source on PCIe0's PIPE mux

On the SM-X710 the PCIe0 link never trains and the controller reports
"Device not found", which drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-designware.c emits only
when the LTSSM sits in DETECT_QUIET/DETECT_ACT -- no link partner is ever seen.

The cause is the GCC PIPE source mux. It powers up selecting the XO reference
rather than the PHY output, and no mainline code ever switches it, so the MAC-PHY
PIPE interface is dead and the LTSSM never performs receiver detection.

Measured on the device before this change:

  pcie0_pipe_clk          125000000   <- what the PHY believes it drives
  gcc_pcie_0_pipe_clk_src  19200000   <- the mux, parked on the 19.2 MHz XO

ULONG_MAX is the clk-regmap-phy-mux sentinel for "select the PHY source", and the
branch's CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT propagates it to the parent mux.

Provenance: adapted from kernel/patches/unpark-pcie0-pipe-mux.patch in the
gts9wifi-fedora-linux port for this same device (commit ab123e7). Downstream, not
upstream; the on-device verification is recorded under reference/boot-tests/. The
fix is not Samsung-specific in substance -- any board whose boot chain parks this
mux needs it -- and belongs upstream once measured.

Not verified on hardware at the time of writing.

---
diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
index d3effad7a..b66468bf7 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-pcie.c
@@ -4981,6 +4981,17 @@ static int qmp_pcie_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The GCC PIPE source muxes power up selecting the PHY output and no
+	 * mainline code switches them, but Samsung's X710 boot chain parks
+	 * PCIe0's mux on the XO reference (the register reads PHY_MUX_REF_SRC,
+	 * 19.2 MHz).  With the mux parked the MAC-PHY PIPE interface is dead and
+	 * the LTSSM never performs receiver detection, so the WCN endpoint
+	 * is never found.  ULONG_MAX is the clk-regmap-phy-mux sentinel for
+	 * "select the PHY source", propagated by the branch's CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT.
+	 */
+	clk_set_rate(qmp->pipe_clks[0].clk, ULONG_MAX);
+
 	ret = reset_control_deassert(qmp->nocsr_reset);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(qmp->dev, "no-csr reset deassert failed\n");
